      ],
      "seo_eligible": true,
      "editorial": {
        "what_changed": "If you want to compete, you need to be multi-model. And if you want to take advantage of everything that different AI models have to offer, you need a great harness. But building one that works seamlessly across multiple models and surfaces is incredibly hard. You need to solve for performance, quality, and cost. And... The post Introducing the Microsoft Copilot harness: Unlocking the potential of truly multi-model agentic work appeared first on The Official Microsoft Blog .",
        "why_it_matters": "Cost changes can alter which workloads are economical to run at scale, especially for high-volume or agentic use. The meaningful signal is not the headline price alone but how the new rates interact with caching, long context, tool use, and production volume.",
        "what_to_verify": "Check the billing unit, context thresholds, cached-input treatment, tool or service charges, regional differences, and the date the new pricing takes effect."
      }
    },
